Factoring \(2026\) gives \(2026 = 2 \times 1013\), where both \(2\) and \(1013\) are prime. Therefore, \(P = 2^{20} \times 1013^{20}\), and the number of positive integer divisors of \(P\) is \((20 + 1)(20 + 1) = 441\).

