The pentagon can be placed on a coordinate plane with \(A = (0, 0)\), \(E = (20, 0)\), \(B = (0, b)\) with \(b = AB > 0\), and \(D = (20, d)\) with \(d = DE > 0\) and \(d < b\). Given \(\angle B = \angle D = 45^\circ\) and \(BC = 14\sqrt{2}\), the coordinates of \(C\) are determined as \(C = (14, b - 14)\) with \(d = b - 8\) to satisfy the angle conditions and ensure the pentagon is nonconvex at \(C\) with \(\angle C = 270^\circ\). The polygon is simple for \(b > 14\).

The area of pentagon \(ABCDE\) computed via the shoelace formula is \(40b - 328\). For the area to be an integer multiple of \(16\), \(40b - 328\) must be divisible by \(16\), which simplifies to \(b\) being odd. Additionally, \(b\) is an integer with \(15 \leq b \leq 2025\) (since \(b > 14\) and \(b < 2026\)). The number of odd integers in this range is \(1006\).

