The three circles of radius 2 have centers on a circle of radius 9 centered at \(O\), since they are internally tangent to the circle \(\Omega\) of radius 11. The chords of \(\Omega\) are tangent to pairs of these circles. Given that two chords have length \(4\sqrt{30}\), the distance from \(O\) to each of these chord lines is \(p = 1\). For the configuration where \(O\) lies inside the triangle formed by the chords, the circles are on the opposite side of each chord from \(O\), leading to \(p = d - 2\), where \(d\) is the distance from \(O\) to the line joining the centers of the corresponding circles. Thus, for the two equal chords, \(d = 3\).

Using the geometry of the centers on the circle of radius 9, the distances from \(O\) to lines joining the centers for the two equal chords are both 3, leading to central angles of \(2\arccos(1/3)\) for the corresponding arcs. The third side has distance \(d_{\text{BC}} = 7\), giving \(p_{\text{BC}} = 7 - 2 = 5\). The chord length is then calculated as \(2\sqrt{11^2 - 5^2} = 2\sqrt{96} = 8\sqrt{6}\).

\boxed{8\sqrt{6}}

The three circles of radius 2 are internally tangent to the circle $\Omega$ of radius 11, so their centers lie on a circle of radius 9 centered at $O$. For each pair of circles, a chord of $\Omega$ is tangent to both circles. Given two chords have length $4\sqrt{30}$, the distance from $O$ to each such chord is $p = 1$, since $2\sqrt{11^2 - p^2} = 4\sqrt{30}$ implies $p = 1$.

For a chord tangent to two circles with centers at angular separation $\Delta$, the distance from $O$ to the chord is $p = 9\cos(\Delta/2) - 2$ when $O$ and the circles are on opposite sides. For the two chords with $p = 1$, this gives $\cos(\Delta/2) = 1/3$, so $\Delta = 2\arccos(1/3)$. With two such equal angular separations, the third separation is $\Delta' = 2\pi - 4\arccos(1/3)$. Then $\cos(\Delta'/2) = \cos(\pi - 2\arccos(1/3)) = -\cos(2\arccos(1/3)) = -(2\cos^2(\arccos(1/3)) - 1) = -(2/9 - 1) = 7/9$. Thus, the distance for the third chord is $p' = 9 \cdot (7/9) - 2 = 5$. The chord length is $2\sqrt{11^2 - 5^2} = 2\sqrt{96} = 8\sqrt{6}$.

\boxed{8\sqrt{6}}

